settings
========

Pyxplot's settings: the values changed by the set command, their defaults,
and the tables of keywords they can take. The settings themselves are held in
the structures defined in settings.h; they are changed by commands/set.c,
displayed by commands/show.c, and read from configuration files by readConf.c.
Several modules split their header in two: a .h file of types, which many
files need, and a _fns.h file of functions.

settings.h
    The structures which hold every setting: those of the output terminal, of
    graphs, of axes and their ticks, and the master ppl_settings structure,
    which holds both the current and the default value of each.

settingsInit.c, settings_fns.h
    Sets every setting to its default value when Pyxplot starts, taking the
    default paper size from the environment or the locale.

settingTypes.c, settingTypes.h
    Tables of the keywords which each setting can take (e.g. the names of the
    plot styles and output terminals), with the abbreviations allowed and the
    numeric codes used internally, and functions to look them up.

arrows.c, arrows.h, arrows_fns.h
    The arrows added to graphs with "set arrow": adding, removing, resetting,
    copying and describing them.

labels.c, labels.h, labels_fns.h
    The text labels added to graphs with "set label", handled in the same way
    as arrows.

axes.c, axes_fns.h
    Freeing, copying and comparing the settings of axes, and converting
    between values along an axis and positions along it.

withWords.c, withWords.h, withWords_fns.h
    The style options which follow "with" in commands such as plot, e.g.
    "with lines color red": reading them from commands, merging them with
    numbered styles, and writing them out as text.

colors.c, colors.h
    Converts the colors given in commands (color objects, palette numbers, or
    expressions to evaluate for each data point) into color components.

epsColors.c, epsColors.h (generated at build time; not in the repository)
    The names and CMYK components of the named colors, generated by
    buildScripts/colorlistGenerate.py.

papersizes.c, papersizes.h
    The table of named paper sizes, such as a4 and letter, and functions to
    look them up.

textConstants.c, textConstants.h
    Fixed texts which Pyxplot displays: its version string, command-line help,
    welcome banner, and the lists of options of set, unset and show.
